module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FiniteLocallyFree.FpqcLocalAtTarget
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteLocallyFreeProper
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Size.Cutoff
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.FiniteHilbert.HilbertCoverPullbackFiber

/-!
# A descended cover of schemes is an object of the fibre of `ℋ_d`

Effectivity of a descent datum of the category `ℋ_d` of degree-`d` finite locally free covers
relative to the sieve generated by a covering family `g i : X i ⟶ T` asks for an object of the
*fibre of `ℋ_d` over `T`* — a cover of `T` by an object of the big fppf site of `S`, finite
locally free of degree `d` — whereas descent of schemes produces a bare scheme `W` over the
scheme underlying `T` together with cartesian squares exhibiting the covers of the datum as its
base changes. This file closes that gap. Three things have to be checked, and none of them is an
assumption:

* the descended morphism is **finite locally free of degree `d`**, because that property is fpqc
  local on the base (`Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_isLocalAtTarget_fpqc`, which is
  Stacks 02VO) and its base changes along the covering family are the covers of the datum;
* the descended scheme is an **object of the big fppf site of `S`**, because a finite locally
  free morphism is of finite type, so the source of one into a scheme below the site's cutoff is
  below the cutoff as well
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_lt_of_locallyOfFiniteType_of_quasiCompact`, which is Stacks 000R
  (5)); no size hypothesis on `W` is made;
* the cartesian squares of schemes are **cartesian in the site**, because the canonical functor
  to schemes reflects fibre products and is faithful.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_isPullback_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`: a morphism
  all of whose base changes along the members of an fpqc covering family are finite locally free
  of degree `d` is finite locally free of degree `d`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.mem_fpqcPrecoverage_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation`: a jointly
  surjective family of flat morphisms locally of finite presentation is an fpqc covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_objectOver_isPullback_of_isPullback_toScheme`: **the
  realization.** A scheme over the scheme underlying `T` whose base changes along a covering
  family are the underlying schemes of degree-`d` covers in the site is itself an object of the
  site, the descended morphism is a degree-`d` cover, and the cartesian squares hold in the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_fiber_isCartesian_of_isPullback_toScheme`: the same read in
  `ℋ_d`, as an object of the fibre over `T` together with a cartesian morphism of `ℋ_d` from each
  cover of the family into it. This is the shape in which
  `CategoryTheory.Functor.SieveDescentDatum.isEffective_of_chosenOverlaps` consumes a descended
  object.

## Implementation notes

The degree and the size bound are read off the *same* family of cartesian squares, and neither
uses the gluing isomorphisms of a descent datum: the content of this file is about one morphism
and its base changes, so it is stated for a bare family of cartesian squares rather than for a
chart of a descent datum. That is also what makes it usable at an index type in an arbitrary
universe, the index type of the covering family being free.

The containment of the descended scheme in the site does not go through
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSite.contains_of_flat_of_surjective`, which asks for a *single* flat
surjective morphism onto it: the base changes of the covering family cover the descended scheme
only jointly, and no coproduct of them need be an object of the site. The finite-type bound of
Stacks 000R (5) applies to the descended morphism itself and needs no such coproduct.

No tag attribute sits on anything here. Reading a descended scheme as an object of the fibre of
`ℋ_d` is bookkeeping internal to the formalisation of Stacks 026F for `ℋ_d`; the two tags the
argument consumes, Stacks 02VO and Stacks 000R (5), carry their attributes where they are proved.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 02VO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02VO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 000R](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/000R)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 026F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/026F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0245](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0245)
-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry

universe u v

namespace Stacks.Morphisms

/-- **The degree of a morphism of schemes may be read off an fpqc covering of the base.** If
every base change of `w` along a member of an fpqc covering family of its target is finite
locally free of degree `d`, then so is `w`.

This is `Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_isLocalAtTarget_fpqc` — Stacks 02VO for a
fixed degree — read at a family of cartesian squares rather than at the chosen fibre products. -/
theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_isPullback_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage {d : ℕ}
    {Ts W : Scheme.{u}} {ι : Type v} {Xs Zs : ι → Scheme.{u}} {gs : ∀ i, Xs i ⟶ Ts}
    {cs : ∀ i, Zs i ⟶ Xs i} (w : W ⟶ Ts) (proj : ∀ i, Zs i ⟶ W)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows Xs gs ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage Ts)
    (hpb : ∀ i, IsPullback (proj i) (cs i) w (gs i))
    (hc : ∀ i, IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank (cs i) d) :
    IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank w d := by
  refine MorphismProperty.IsLocalAtTarget.of_forall_pullbackSnd
    (P := IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.property.{u} d) hcov ?_
  rintro U g _ ⟨i⟩
  have key : IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.property.{u} d ((hpb i).isoPullback.inv ≫ cs i) :=
    (MorphismProperty.cancel_left_of_respectsIso
      (IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.property.{u} d) (hpb i).isoPullback.inv (cs i)).mpr (hc i)
  rwa [(hpb i).isoPullback_inv_snd] at key

end Stacks.Morphisms

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **A jointly surjective family of flat morphisms locally of finite presentation is an fpqc
covering family.** Such a family is an fppf covering family, and every fppf covering family is an
fpqc covering family by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fppfPrecoverage_le_fpqcPrecoverage`. -/
theorem mem_fpqcPrecoverage_of_flat_of_locallyOfFinitePresentation {Ts : Scheme.{u}}
    {ι : Type v} {Xs : ι → Scheme.{u}} (gs : ∀ i, Xs i ⟶ Ts)
    (hflat : ∀ i, Flat (gs i)) (hlfp : ∀ i, LocallyOfFinitePresentation (gs i))
    (hsurj : ∀ x : Ts, ∃ i, x ∈ Set.range (gs i)) :
    Presieve.ofArrows Xs gs ∈ Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage Ts := by
  refine Scheme.fppfPrecoverage_le_fpqcPrecoverage _ ?_
  rw [Scheme.fppfPrecoverage, Scheme.ofArrows_mem_precoverage_iff]
  exact ⟨hsurj, fun i ↦ ⟨hflat i, hlfp i⟩⟩

namespace Stack

attribute [local implicit_reducible] finiteCoverProjection CategoryTheory.Functor.Fiber

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S} {d : ℕ}

/-- **A cover descended as a scheme is a cover in the big fppf site of `S`.** Let
`g i : X i ⟶ T` be a family of morphisms of the big fppf site of `S` whose underlying family of
morphisms of schemes is an fpqc covering, let `c i : Zo i ⟶ X i` be degree-`d` finite locally
free covers, and suppose a scheme `W` over the scheme underlying `T` has the underlying scheme of
`Zo i` as its base change along the underlying morphism of `g i`, for every `i`. Then `W` carries
the structure of an object of the big fppf site of `S` over `T`, the descended morphism is a
degree-`d` finite locally free cover, and `Zo i` is its base change along `g i` *in the site*.

The degree is `Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_isPullback_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage`,
the size bound is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_lt_of_locallyOfFiniteType_of_quasiCompact` at
the descended morphism — which is of finite type, being finite locally free — and the cartesian
squares transfer back because the canonical functor to schemes reflects fibre products and is
faithful.

The object produced is a *lift* of the given data, not merely some object with the same
properties: under an isomorphism `e` identifying the underlying scheme of the produced object
with `W`, the descended morphism is `w` itself and each projection is `proj i`. Those two
identifications are part of the conclusion, because a further compatibility of the projections
— say the one a chart of a descent datum carries — is a statement about `proj`, and the only
route from it to the corresponding statement in the site is through them and the faithfulness
of the canonical functor. -/
theorem exists_objectOver_isPullback_of_isPullback_toScheme
    {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} {ι : Type v} {X Zo : ι → BigFppfOver B S hS}
    {g : ∀ i, X i ⟶ T} {c : ∀ i, Zo i ⟶ X i}
    (hc : ∀ i, Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c i)) d)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (X i))
      (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i)) ∈
        Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T))
    {W : Scheme.{u}} (w : W ⟶ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
    (proj : ∀ i, (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Zo i) ⟶ W)
    (hpb : ∀ i, IsPullback (proj i) ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c i)) w
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i))) :
    ∃ (Wo : BigFppfOver B S hS) (wo : Wo ⟶ T) (pr : ∀ i, Zo i ⟶ Wo)
      (e : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Wo ≅ W),
      Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
          ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map wo) d ∧
        (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map wo = e.hom ≫ w ∧
        (∀ i, (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (pr i) ≫ e.hom = proj i) ∧
        ∀ i, IsPullback (pr i) (c i) wo (g i) := by
  have hw : Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank w d :=
    Stacks.Morphisms.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_of_isPullback_of_mem_fpqcPrecoverage
      w proj hcov hpb hc
  have : IsFinite w := Stacks.Morphisms.isFinite_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank w d
  have hWc : B.Contains W :=
    Scheme.size_lt_of_locallyOfFiniteType_of_quasiCompact w T.left.property
  -- the descended scheme as an object of the site, over `T`
  let Wleft : B.Schemes := B.obj hWc
  let w' : Wleft ⟶ T.left := B.inclusion.preimage w
  have hw' : B.inclusion.map w' = w :=
    B.inclusion.map_preimage (X := Wleft) (Y := T.left) w
  let Wo : BigFppfOver B S hS := Over.mk (w' ≫ T.hom)
  let wo : Wo ⟶ T := Over.homMk w'
  have hwo : (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map wo = w := hw'
  -- the projections, lifted to the site
  let pr' : ∀ i, (Zo i).left ⟶ Wleft := fun i ↦ B.inclusion.preimage (proj i)
  have hpr' : ∀ i, B.inclusion.map (pr' i) = proj i := fun i ↦
    B.inclusion.map_preimage (X := (Zo i).left) (Y := Wleft) (proj i)
  have hsq : ∀ i, pr' i ≫ w' = (c i).left ≫ (g i).left := by
    intro i
    refine B.inclusion.map_injective ?_
    rw [B.inclusion.map_comp, B.inclusion.map_comp, hpr' i, hw']
    exact (hpb i).w
  let pr : ∀ i, Zo i ⟶ Wo := fun i ↦ Over.homMk (pr' i) (by
    change pr' i ≫ w' ≫ T.hom = (Zo i).hom
    rw [← Category.assoc, hsq i, Category.assoc, Over.w (g i), Over.w (c i)])
  refine ⟨Wo, wo, pr, Iso.refl ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj Wo),
    by rwa [hwo], by simpa using hwo, fun i ↦ (Category.comp_id _).trans (hpr' i), fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  refine IsPullback.of_map_of_faithful (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS) ?_
  rw [show (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (pr i) = proj i from hpr' i, hwo]
  exact hpb i

/-- **A cover descended as a scheme is an object of the fibre of `ℋ_d` over `T`, and every cover
of the family maps cartesianly into it.** This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_objectOver_isPullback_of_isPullback_toScheme` read in the
category of degree-`d` finite locally free covers: a cartesian square over `g i` *is* a morphism
of `ℋ_d` lying over `g i`, and every morphism of `ℋ_d` is cartesian over its base component by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCartesian_of_isHomLift`.

This is the shape in which
`CategoryTheory.Functor.SieveDescentDatum.isEffective_of_chosenOverlaps` consumes a descended
object: it asks for an object of the fibre over the base of the sieve together with a cartesian
morphism out of each object of the datum. -/
theorem exists_fiber_isCartesian_of_isPullback_toScheme
    {T : BigFppfOver B S hS} {ι : Type v} {X Zo : ι → BigFppfOver B S hS}
    {g : ∀ i, X i ⟶ T} {c : ∀ i, Zo i ⟶ X i}
    (hc : ∀ i, Stacks.Morphisms.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c i)) d)
    (hcov : Presieve.ofArrows (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (X i))
      (fun i ↦ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i)) ∈
        Scheme.fpqcPrecoverage ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T))
    {W : Scheme.{u}} (w : W ⟶ (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj T)
    (proj : ∀ i, (BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj (Zo i) ⟶ W)
    (hpb : ∀ i, IsPullback (proj i) ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (c i)) w
      ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).map (g i))) :
    ∃ (a : (finiteCoverProjection (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (d := d)).Fiber T)
      (ζ : ∀ i, (⟨X i, Zo i, c i, hc i⟩ : FiniteCover B S hS d) ⟶ a.1),
      ∀ i, (finiteCoverProjection (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (d := d)).IsCartesian
        (g i) (ζ i) := by
  obtain ⟨Wo, wo, pr, -, hwo, -, -, hsq⟩ :=
    exists_objectOver_isPullback_of_isPullback_toScheme (d := d) hc hcov w proj hpb
  refine ⟨⟨⟨T, Wo, wo, hwo⟩, rfl⟩, fun i ↦ ⟨g i, pr i, hsq i⟩, fun i ↦ ?_⟩
  refine isCartesian_of_isHomLift (g i) _ ?_
  refine CategoryTheory.IsHomLift.of_fac'
    (finiteCoverProjection (B := B) (S := S) (hS := hS) (d := d)) (g i) _ rfl rfl ?_
  change g i = eqToHom rfl ≫ g i ≫ eqToHom rfl
  simp

end Stack

end AlgebraicGeometry

end

end
